;;; A name written **only in a rule's `:match`** never became a candidate —
;;; M1e2 **W15**, register row `W15/match-only` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`),
;;; owned by S1e2.2.14. Banked from S1e2.2.4's residue probe of 2026-11-04.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; W4's program (`../alive-set-fresh-name.ein`) with its `spawn` rule replaced
;;; by `reach-z`, which names `Z` in its `:match` and not in its `:assert`.
;;; `Z` is in no fact and in no `:assert`, so it was neither in the KB's names
;;; nor in what S1e2.2.4 seeded the blind enumerator with (a rule's `:assert`
;;; constants), and the candidates were `q` over `A` and `B` alone.
;;;
;;;   `no-a` / `no-b` refute every `q` that points at A or at B.
;;;   `reach-z` says what reaching Z means; the query asks it.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `solution_semantics.md` § 1.2: a name is *a constant the program mentions,
;;; in a fact or in a rule*, and the user ruled on 2026-11-04 that this is
;;; meant literally (Q-M1e2.9 (a)): a constant anywhere in a rule, `:match`
;;; included, is a name of the program and so a candidate object. So H is the
;;; six `q` candidates over A, B and Z, four of them dead alone, and
;;; `{(q A Z), (q B Z)}` saturates to a consistent, quiescent state (`reach-z`
;;; adds `(good A)` and `(good B)`) and is the maximal one: R is ∅,
;;; `{(q A Z)}`, `{(q B Z)}` and both — `match-only-declared.ein`'s R, which
;;; names `Z` in a fact.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answers today ──────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; H is 2 candidates, `(q A B)` and `(q B A)`, both dead alone, and R is
;;; `{∅}`: root itself, one state (`ein solve FILE`, 2026-11-04). The register
;;; row holds that run until S1e2.2.14's fix, and the fixing commit gives
;;; this file the `(solve … :expect (region …))` that states R.

(relation p T T)
(relation q T T)
(relation good T)

(p A B)

(rule reach-z ()
  :match  (q ?a Z)
  :assert (good ?a)
  :why    "{?a} reaches Z")

(rule no-a ()
  :match  (q ?x A)
  :assert (false)
  :why    "nothing may reach A")

(rule no-b ()
  :match  (q ?x B)
  :assert (false)
  :why    "nothing may reach B")

(solve
  :no-hypothesis (p good))

(query
  :goal   (good ?a))
